  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula a cd:MathExpression ; skos:prefLabel "Precision weights and Welch reference"@en ; cd:body "Precision weights and Welch reference"@en ; cd:latex "\\begin{aligned}w_i&=n_i/s_i^2,&W&=\\sum_i w_i,&\\bar y_w&=\\sum_i w_i\\bar y_i/W\\\\U&=\\sum_i(1-w_i/W)^2/(n_i-1)\\\\F_W&=\\frac{\\sum_i w_i(\\bar y_i-\\bar y_w)^2/(k-1)}{1+2(k-2)U/(k^2-1)},&\\nu_2&=\\frac{k^2-1}{3U}\\end{aligned}" ; dct:hasPart ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-legend ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; skos:prefLabel "Symbols"@en ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-1, ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-2, ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-3 ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-legend .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-1 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Groups and units"@en ; cd:body "i indexes k = 3 independent groups; nᵢ is their sample size; ȳᵢ is mean recovery (%) and sᵢ² is sample variance (pp²)."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-2 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Weights"@en ; cd:body "wᵢ is inverse estimated variance of the group mean (pp⁻²); W is total weight and ȳ_w is the weighted mean in percent. U is a dimensionless correction."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-3 a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Test and notation"@en ; cd:body "F_W is the dimensionless Welch statistic; its approximate reference has numerator df k−1 and denominator df ν₂. Σ sums over groups, / and fraction bars divide, juxtaposition multiplies, superscript 2 squares, and −, + and = denote subtraction, addition and equality."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula-symbol-3 .
