  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-16-formula .
  ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-test-chain ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-test-chain ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-3 .
  ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-conclusion ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-4 .
  ex:l7-scene17-calc a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-1, ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-2, ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-3, ex:l7-teaching-17-calc-4 ; cd:narration "Start with the two sums of squares. They have different degrees of freedom, so first turn them into mean squares. The method term gives 84 divided by 2, or 42. The residual term gives 30 divided by 15, or 2. Their ratio is the observed F of 21. Under equal population means and the classical model assumptions, compare that ratio with an F distribution on 2 and 15 degrees of freedom. The probability in its right tail beyond 21 is about 0.00004484. The next slide collects exactly these quantities into one ANOVA table."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene17-calc .
  ex:l7-teaching-22-question-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-22-question-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-22-question-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-22-question-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-explained-question ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-22-question-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-22-question-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-22-question-conclusion ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-22-question-3 .
  ex:l7-scene22-question a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-teaching-22-question-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-teaching-22-question-1, ex:l7-teaching-22-question-2, ex:l7-teaching-22-question-3 ; cd:narration "A small p-value tells us how unusual the F statistic is under the null model. It does not tell us how much of the observed variation the fitted methods account for. Start with the total: every preparation differs from the grand mean. Once each method gets its own fitted mean, we can distinguish changes in those means from the departures left within each method. The first part belongs to the model; the second is residual variation, which can include measurement noise and omitted sources of variation. Compare their sizes before deciding whether the effect is useful in practice."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene22-question .
  ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-tukey-range ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-tukey-adjusted ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-3 .
  ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-conclusion ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-4 .
  ex:l7-scene26-adjusted a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-1, ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-2, ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-3, ex:l7-teaching-26-adjusted-4 ; cd:narration "For B minus A, the difference is four percentage points. Standardize its absolute value using the pooled residual mean square and the common sample size. This gives q about 6.928. Instead of using the reference for one isolated pair, compare with the studentized range of three means. Under the common-mean reference this range tracks the largest standardized gap available among the pairs. Its upper-tail probability beyond our q is about 0.000532. This is why the p-value already accounts for the family. The same reference gives simultaneous intervals, which the next slide shows."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene26-adjusted .
  ex:l7-teaching-31-formula a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-marginal ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-31-formula .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-table ; cd:communicativeRole cd:TableRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasTableRow" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-welch-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-3 .
  ex:l7-teaching-40-example-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-conclusion ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-40-example-4 .
  ex:l7-scene40-example a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-teaching-40-example-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-teaching-40-example-1, ex:l7-teaching-40-example-2, ex:l7-teaching-40-example-3, ex:l7-teaching-40-example-4 ; cd:narration "All three groups have the same sample size, but their variances differ. For A and C the variance is 3.5 squared percentage points, so each weight is about 1.714. For B it is 56, so B's weight is only about 0.107. Welch uses these weights for its mean comparison and adjusts the reference degrees of freedom. Here the statistic is 3.786, with 2 numerator and about 9.06 denominator degrees of freedom. The upper-tail probability is 0.064. At a preselected 0.05 threshold this example does not reject equality of means. That decision is specific to this dataset."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene40-example .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:level7-anova-kw-rank-sums ; cd:communicativeRole cd:MediaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:uri" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-kw-formula ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-3 .
  ex:l7-teaching-41-example-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-conclusion ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-41-example-4 .
  ex:l7-scene41-example a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-teaching-41-example-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-teaching-41-example-1, ex:l7-teaching-41-example-2, ex:l7-teaching-41-example-3, ex:l7-teaching-41-example-4 ; cd:narration "Large differences between rank sums raise the test statistic. The two tied observations require a correction before evaluating H. In this toy example H is 4.191. With only six observations, use the exact reference: hold the observed ranks fixed and enumerate all ninety allocations of two observations to each of three labelled groups. 12 allocations reach or exceed our statistic, so the exact p-value is 0.133. The usual large-sample chi-square approximation gives 0.123 here. Keep the exact result for this small example and use the plot to see which groups drove the rank separation."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene41-example .
  ex:l7-teaching-42-model-1 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-42-model-heading ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-42-model-1 .
  ex:l7-teaching-42-model-2 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 2 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-manova-table ; cd:communicativeRole cd:TableRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:hasTableRow" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-42-model-2 .
  ex:l7-teaching-42-model-3 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 3 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-manova-null ; cd:communicativeRole cd:FormulaRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:latex" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-42-model-3 .
  ex:l7-teaching-42-model-4 a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 4 ; cd:selectsResource ex:l7-teaching-42-model-conclusion ; cd:communicativeRole cd:StatementRole ; cd:selectionPath "cd:body" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-teaching-42-model-4 .
  ex:l7-scene42-model a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:l7-teaching-42-model-focus ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:l7-teaching-42-model-1, ex:l7-teaching-42-model-2, ex:l7-teaching-42-model-3, ex:l7-teaching-42-model-4 ; cd:narration "The null hypothesis says that the two-dimensional population mean vector is the same for all three SPE methods. The test compares separation among the fitted group centers with the spread and correlation left within each group. For these illustrative paired recoveries the Pillai trace is 1.414; the approximate F statistic is 18.077 with 4 and 30 degrees of freedom, giving p about 1.18e-07. The classical model needs independent preparations, multivariate normal errors and a common within-group covariance matrix. A small p-value is evidence of a joint difference; it does not identify a particular analyte or method pair."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:l7-source-package ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:l7-source-package cd:supportsResource ex:l7-scene42-model .
}
